            <ArticleTitle>Structure and bonding of [Pd2Sn18]4-: an interesting example of the mutual delocalisation phenomenon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2214-2219</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6dt04561h</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this article, we have presented a computational analysis on the structure and bonding of [Pd2Sn18]4- and illustrated that it serves as an interesting example of OMO-UMO mutual delocalisation with two identical [PdE9]2- fragments. We have also illustrated the alternative roles that could be played by an [ME9]2-/[E9]2- fragment, a simple L-type donor and a lone-pair acceptor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
